course: dictionary
lesson: 1107
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them tell you which meaning is right. Brat is informal, so you will hear it in chats and stories more than in school books. «Stop being such a brat, Sam!» said Mum, when he grabbed the last biscuit. Mum is cross, so brat means a child who behaves badly.
explain: Brat has other meanings too. An army brat is a child who moved from base to base because a parent was in the armed forces. Friends sometimes use brat jokingly about a younger person who is annoying. Ask yourself: does my meaning fit the sentence? If it does, you have found the right one.
explain: Brat is also a family word in other languages. In Ukrainian, «brat» means brother, as in «tse miy brat», which means "that's my brother". The same spelling can mean something very different in another language, so always check the context first.
fact: «Brat» means a child who behaves badly, is spoiled or rude.
fact: An «army brat» is a child who moves from base to base because a parent is in the armed forces.
fact: Adding -y makes «bratty», an adjective meaning like a brat: «a bratty little sister».
fact: In Ukrainian, «brat» means brother, and «dvoyurodnyi brat» means male cousin.
exercise: «Stop being such a brat, Sam!» What does brat mean here? | A brother in Ukrainian | A kind and helpful helper | * A child who behaves badly and is rude | A military base
exercise: What is an army brat? | A kind teacher at school | A child who wins every race | A soldier who lives in a tent | * A child who moved from base to base because a parent was in the armed forces
exercise: In Ukrainian, «tse miy brat» means what? | Let's go to the park | A big family dinner | * That's my brother | A cousin who lives far away
test: Which word is the adjective form of brat? | brattish | * bratty | bratting | bratful
test: Ella's big brother teases her: «You little brat!» He is laughing as he says it. Why is it a joke? | * He is playfully teasing her, because brat can be used jokingly about an annoying younger person | He is serious and very angry | He wants a new brother | He means she is a soldier
exam: Read: «The army brat unpacked her boxes again, in a new town.» What does army brat mean? | * A child who moves often because a parent is in the army | A brave grown-up soldier | A child who is rude and spoiled | A soldier's friend who works in a shop
